# Forced NXDOMAIN. Evaluated ahead of any allow entry of lower specificity.
#
# IMPORTANT dnsmasq semantic: an allow entry matches the domain AND every
# subdomain of it. So `github.com` in 10-github.list implicitly permits every
# *.github.com host. Anything under an allowed parent that you do NOT want
# has to be named here explicitly -- that is what this file is for.
#
# Copilot. api.githubcopilot.com is a CNAME to glb-*.github.com, which lands
# in 140.82.112.0/20 -- GitHub's own range -- so hostname denial is the only
# thing that actually stops it.
githubcopilot.com
copilot-proxy.githubusercontent.com
copilot-telemetry.githubusercontent.com
copilot-telemetry-service.githubusercontent.com

# Tarball/zip endpoint. Reachable only as a side effect of allowing
# github.com; git clone/pull/push never touch it.
codeload.github.com
